# /opt/gexbot/gexbot.env      chmod 600
# All times are CENTRAL.

GEXBOT_HOME=/opt/gexbot/data

# ── symbols ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GEXBOT_SYMBOLS=SPY,QQQ

# ── what to trade ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# spread — debit vertical. Cheaper per contract, both legs decay together so
#          theta is partly hedged, upside capped at the width.
#          MULTI-LEG: requires Robinhood options level 3.
# single — one long call (long signal) or put (short signal). Full premium,
#          full theta, uncapped upside.
#          SINGLE-LEG: requires only options level 2.
#
# Identical entry logic either way — same gamma zones, same 13 checks, same
# stop and target percentages on premium. Only the instrument differs.
# The measured evidence in HANDOFF.md is all spreads; singles are untested.
#
GEXBOT_STRUCTURE=spread

# Where the long strike sits relative to spot: itm | atm | otm
#   itm  closest breakeven, most premium per contract
#   otm  cheapest per contract, furthest breakeven
# OTM buys affordability with win rate, not with edge — on the tested sample an
# ATM 0DTE contract won only 35% because breakeven sat above the median winning
# move, and OTM pushes breakeven further out still. On a small account it is
# often the only way to hold a contract at all, which is a fair reason to use
# it. "It's cheap" is not.
GEXBOT_MONEYNESS=itm

# ── session clock (CENTRAL) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# When the bot may OPEN a trade. Regular hours are 08:30–15:00 CT.
# 08:35 skips the opening auction candle.
#
# 08:35–09:30 is the original window and the one the 27% trigger rate in
# HANDOFF.md was measured on. Widening it is a change of strategy, not a
# setting: more bars evaluated, more triggers, and a different mix of setups,
# since midday chop is not the opening drive. None of that is measured.
#
# It is coherent with dated contracts. A 0DTE opened at 13:45 has 45 minutes
# before the 14:30 force-flat, and short holds lost money at every DTE on the
# tested sample. A 1DTE+ held overnight has no force-flat at all, so a late
# entry has days to work. The bot warns at startup if the window ends less
# than an hour before a force-flat that actually applies.
GEXBOT_ENTRY_START=08:35
GEXBOT_ENTRY_END=14:00

# Close 0DTE by this time. Ignored when the position is held overnight, but a
# contract is ALWAYS flattened on its own expiry date regardless.
GEXBOT_FORCE_FLAT=14:30

# Trades per symbol per day. A wider entry window makes this the real limit on
# how often the bot acts.
GEXBOT_MAX_TRADES=1

# ── expiry / DTE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which expiry to TRADE. 0 = same day, 1 = next session, 7 = a week out.
# Never resolves shorter than requested — asking for 3 on a Friday gets you
# Monday, not that afternoon.
GEXBOT_TRADE_DTE=1

# Which expiries feed the MAP. Near-dated gamma drives intraday hedging
# pressure whatever you hold, so aggregate the front expiries regardless of
# what you trade.
GEXBOT_MAP_DTE_MAX=7

# Required for TRADE_DTE > 0, otherwise the 14:30 force-flat closes it same day.
GEXBOT_HOLD_OVERNIGHT=yes

# ── authorization ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The daemon holds its own OAuth grant — a Claude connector authorizes Claude,
# not this process. Authorize once with:  gexbot.py --login
# Tokens land in $GEXBOT_HOME/oauth (0600) and refresh silently after that.
#
# Port the browser redirect comes back on. Forward it from the machine running
# the browser:  ssh -L 8788:127.0.0.1:8788 root@your-vps
GEXBOT_OAUTH_PORT=8788
# Leave blank unless you know Robinhood's exact scope strings; blank means the
# server applies its default grant.
GEXBOT_OAUTH_SCOPE=

# ── account ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed when arming. --login prints the account numbers it can see.
GEXBOT_ACCOUNT=
# Drives position sizing: 1% of this is risked per trade.
GEXBOT_ACCOUNT_VALUE=25000

# ── sizing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two different numbers. Keep them straight:
#
#   ALLOC_PCT  how much of the account is SPENT on premium
#   loss       what is LOST if the stop hits = ALLOC_PCT x 45%
#
# Allocation is the control; the loss follows from it. 80% deployed means 36%
# of the account gone on a stop-out — two of those roughly halve it. That is a
# bet-sizing decision, not position sizing. It is survivable only because the
# bot takes one trade per symbol per day and the daily stop halts the session.
#
# 10% is the sane default. A small "challenge" account cannot use the 1% rule
# at all: 1% of $1,000 is $10, which buys $0.22 of premium — no contract exists
# at that price and the bot would simply never trade.
GEXBOT_ALLOC_PCT=0.10

# Optional SECOND ceiling on loss-at-stop. Leave blank and allocation alone
# governs. Set it only for a cap tighter than ALLOC_PCT x 45%.
GEXBOT_RISK_PCT=

# Backstop against a mispriced contract producing an absurd order.
GEXBOT_MAX_CONTRACTS=20

# ── risk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Halt for the rest of the day past this realized loss. Set it BELOW one
# stop-out or it can never fire. On a $1,000 account at 80% allocation, a
# stop-out is ~$360, so ~200 halts you after a single bad trade.
GEXBOT_DAILY_STOP=500
# Leave blank to derive from spot and DTE (recommended).
# GEXBOT_SPREAD_WIDTH=
# GEXBOT_ITM_OFFSET=

# ── dashboard ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GEXBOT_DASH_PORT=8787

# Where to bind:
#   127.0.0.1   this machine only. Reach it with an SSH tunnel:
#                 ssh -L 8787:127.0.0.1:8787 root@your-vps
#               Requires the tunnel to stay open, so no phone access.
#   tailscale   binds this machine's tailnet address. Reachable from any
#               device on your tailnet — phone included — and from nowhere
#               else. No open ports, nothing exposed to the internet.
#               Install: curl -fsSL https://tailscale.com/install.sh | sh
#                        tailscale up
#   0.0.0.0     binds EVERY interface including the public IP. Refused unless
#               GEXBOT_DASH_ALLOW_PUBLIC=yes, because this page shows your
#               positions and a shared token is not enough to put in front of
#               a funded account.
GEXBOT_DASH_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Required for anything other than 127.0.0.1. Generated by install.sh.
# Append it once as ?k=... and it is stored in a cookie for 30 days.
GEXBOT_DASH_TOKEN=

# Only set this if you have genuinely decided to expose the dashboard to the
# internet. Tailscale is the better answer in almost every case.
# GEXBOT_DASH_ALLOW_PUBLIC=yes

# ── alerts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GEXBOT_ALERT_EMAIL=
GEXBOT_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
GEXBOT_SMTP_USER=
GEXBOT_SMTP_PASS=

# ── arming ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Live trading needs BOTH this line uncommented AND --live on the command
# line. Two switches, on purpose. Leave it commented until the paper log
# says something the 56-session sample couldn't.
# GEXBOT_ARMED=yes
